{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1348820-peach-cooking-charms","id":1348820,"title":"[PEACH] Cooking Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-16T03:01:13-08:00","id":1348820,"title":"[PEACH] Cooking Charms","content":"As you can guess, some cooking charms. One word of commentary: I know that the effects of the charms are very strong, perhaps stronger than usually in the book, but I think that generally 3rd edition went too far in nerfing social charms and I generally prefer the design philosophy where effects you can obtain are obviously very strong, but are limited by being very situational or once per story. I know that this is not exactly the design philosophy of Ex3, hence &quot;Apocryphal&quot; keyword.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Harmony of Perfectly Balanced Flavours </b><br /> Cost: 6m<br /> Mins: Craft(cooking) 4, Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Apocryphal<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite None<br /> <br /> In the days of their glory, the Solars where kings, savants, and lawgivers, not servants. However, upon rare occasions, they would honor the guest with a meal which they prepared themselves, surpassing the skills of best mortal cooks. If an Exalt uses this long-forgotten technique, whoever taste the first bit of their perfectly-balanced unique flavours, cannot help but indulge the moment and forget about soul-stirring worries.<br /> <br /> When a character eats a meal prepared using this charm, his Guile is lowered by 2 and his Resolve is lowered by [Solar\u2019s Essence] against all attempts to persuade him to abandon the course of action which would cause immediate problems or be tiresome. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Feast of Gods</b><br /> Cost: 4m / 8m, 1wp<br /> Mins: Craft(cooking) 5, Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Apocryphal<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite: Harmony of Perfectly Balanced Flavours<br /> <br /> When kings of old prepared their sumptuous feasts, it was not uncommon that gods and spirits where visitors to their courts. Meditating on the limitations of body, they managed to prepare meals which transcends these limits.<br /> <br /> This charm has two effects. For 4 motes enables Solar to prepare a meal which might be consumed by any kind of creature which is vaguely able to physically eat: materialised gods, ghosts, strange folk, elementals made of crystal, automata of the First Age, and denizens of strange places for which Second Age has no name. The meal is extremely tasteful to whomever consumes it, even it the consuming party is normally incapable of feeling taste. In addition, the meal prepared using this charm cannot be poisoned at all by any mundane poison and all rolls to resist magical poisons delivered in the meal are granted [Solar\u2019s Essence] automatic non-charm successes. <br /> <br /> Once per story, by paying 8m, 1 wp this charm may be used to enhance persuade attempts. If Solar persuades someone to abandon the given course of violent action, seek for mild pleasures or enjoy the idle and calm life, the attempt is automatically successful against characters of Essence no greater than [Solar\u2019s Essence]. Against characters of Essence greater than that of Solar, this charm grants [Essence] non-charm dice instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T06:24:04-08:00","id":1348848,"title":"","content":"How about instead of potentially wiping out 5 Resolve and 2 Guile (and I\u2019m still not sure why Solar nachos would destroy your poker face), you go with something like, \u201cThe Solar can take a Persuade action to convince the eater to undertake an Inconvenient task without a roll; if the eater would invoke a Decision Point, he treats the Solar\u2019s meal as if it were a Major Intimacy?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T08:33:53-08:00","id":1348863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1348820-peach-cooking-charms?p=1348848#post1348848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u201cThe Solar can take a Persuade action to convince the eater to undertake an Inconvenient task without a roll; if the eater would invoke a Decision Point, he treats the Solar\u2019s meal as if it were a Major Intimacy?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I probably did poor job of explaining what the intention of the first charm is. I would definitely not like to make the effects of this charm too generic and &quot;undertake an Inconvenient task without a roll&quot; is not the intended scope of the charm.<br /> <br /> I rather envisaged that after enjoying a delightful feast with hours and hours of pleasant flavours, you are so softened that you just cannot convince yourself to go to this pesky travel or are not really in the mood to pursue your family vendetta even though you know you should. The same applies to &quot;poker face.&quot; <br /> <br /> Note that wiping out resolve 5 is only when you reach Essence 5 and this a Solar charm. At this point, you are wiping out whole nations with your research and melting down cities. Lowering resolve is essentially the same as non-charm successes but probably more vulnerable to Integrity charms, since lots of them remove penalties. <br /> <br /> I know that this bonus is big, I initially considered something like giving automatic Major Intimacy representing idly pleasant mood, but I am afraid that it might too weak effect, given how extremely situational this charm is. You have to get someone eat your food which you prepared yourself. This is extremely problematic not only when applied to your enemies, but also when you are in a formal enviroment or when you are a guest in a traditional community. Really, this takes some effort to use this charm and I would like for it to really do something when the conditions are met.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T13:35:32-08:00","id":1348919,"title":"","content":"Well if it's a fat and lazy charm you're going to want some kind of duration. Try using Celestial Bliss trick as your guidepost in this regard. You can absolutely make it a Defining Intimacy, but it should probably be easier to resist than Celestial Bliss Trick. Maybe the target has the intimacy so long as the feasting and festivities continue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T15:19:09-08:00","id":1348942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1348820-peach-cooking-charms?p=1348919#post1348919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if it's a fat and lazy charm you're going to want some kind of duration. [...] Maybe the target has the intimacy so long as the feasting and festivities continue.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, thank you. This is how I was thinking about the standard use of the charms back in my head, but it definitely should be incorporated in the charm's text.<br /> <br /> The only part I don't quite agree with is that it should be easier to resist than Celestial Bliss. In many circumstances (and ones typical for Exalted, like in a court) seducing someone can be in fact easier to arrange than preparing a meal yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 11-16-2019, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}